Use these tips to solve problems with bad video: Verify Windows display settings. Try using the native resolution for the LCD panel. This resolution will be the highest resolution available unless the wrong video 
drivers are installed. Try adjusting the brightness, which is a function of the backlight component of the LCD panel. Try updating the video drivers. Download the latest drivers 
