A flickering screen can be caused by bad video drivers, a low refresh rate, a bad inverter, or loose connections inside the laptop. To adjust the refresh rate, use Control Panel 
to open the Display window. In the Display window, click Change display settings. In the Screen Resolution window, click Advanced settings. On the Monitor tab, select the 
